think The live green edge is Season G's scene-read family. Last lap built image/object_relation.rye (a PAIR read). The card and newest log both name the crux-first next rung: a directional/containment SCENE GRAPH joining object_relation over every pair -- the most Lindy-durable of the named candidates, a relational primitive read for years.
think Read the three parents to compose correctly: object_relation.rye (Relation struct, boxes_overlap, nearest_chebyshev, refusals SameObject/BadObjectLabel), scene_manifest.rye (ObjectEntry boxes, Manifest, object_of), and the object_relation witness template (native contains, REDS #85).
think Designed one scene to carry BOTH decisive facts at once -- three nested bracket-L / dot objects whose BOXES nest (big-L (1,1)-(9,9) contains middle-L (3,3)-(7,7) contains dot (5,5)), each child disjoint from its box parent by 2 pixels. Hand-verified distinctness and boxes before coding: big-L pixels at x=1 and y=9, middle-L at x=3 and y=7 (nearest 2 apart), dot at (5,5) 2 from middle-L, 4 from big-L.
think Two cruxes fall out of that one scene: box_parent builds a clean three-level forest choosing each child's TIGHTEST containing box (dot->middle-L not big-L, proving immediate-parent selection over any ancestor), yet object_relation proves each child sits 2 apart from its box parent -- the forest OVER-CLAIMS enclosure, frames not substance. And nearest_neighbor is DIRECTED: dot->middle-L (2), middle-L->big-L (2, earlier label on the tie), NOT dot -- an object can be someone's nearest without their being its own; the middle-L/big-L tie also tests deterministic tie-break by earliest label.
think Bounded before a byte: object count capped at scene_graph_max_objects=256, so the relation matrix (count squared) and build loop are bounded; each cell an object_relation call already bounded by the pixel ceiling. Refuses TooManyObjects past the cap, BadObjectLabel for background/past-count/self, NoNeighbor for a single-object graph -- all having built or read nothing.
obs GREEN on the FIRST full metal run, no reds -- the hand-verified fixtures and the bounded design held; no braces in the print format string and no compound asserts, avoiding the traps earlier scene-read laps hit.
